\begin{abstract}
UPAS-X is a high-precision astrophysical simulation engine capable of modeling 
multi-body shadow geometry, relativistic ephemerides, and HDR flux fields at 
billion-point spatial scales. Combining a 15th-order symplectic integrator, 
analytic ray--cone geometry, and distributed BVH spatial partitioning across 
128 NVIDIA H100 GPUs, UPAS-X achieves numerical stability and throughput beyond 
existing eclipse solvers and photometric pipelines. Validation against NASA GSFC 
eclipse maps, JPL HORIZONS ephemerides, and Gaia/Kepler limb-darkening data 
demonstrates its physical accuracy and reproducibility. UPAS-X establishes a new 
computational standard for eclipse prediction, exoplanet transit modeling, and 
multi-body dynamical systems.
\end{abstract}